description:
Found s504 by s501t (t/op/gmagic.t row 35 "number of stores when chomping a ref", measured while splicing op/gmagic.t for Fable).  PRE-EXISTING: same on main b7ec0093.

Reproducer (perl prints `n=1 ref= [foo]`; PCL prints `n=0 ref=o [foo\n]`):
    package o { use overload q("") => sub { "foo\n" } }
    my $c = bless [], "o"; my $n = chomp $c; print "n=$n ref=", ref($c), " [$c]\n";
perl's chomp works on the STRING value of the operand (pp_chomp: SvPV_force), so an overloaded object is stringified, the newline removed and the result STORED (a tied scalar sees that second STORE -- gmagic.t:62 expects 1 fetch / 2 stores).  PCL's p-chomp-one treats a reference as having no trailing newline.  Layer: runtime p-chomp-one / p-chop-one (one predicate for both); sibling of #119/#402 (the stringify-instead-of-overload shortcuts).
